{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\cdot (3F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=(2yx+{x}^{2})\\,i+(5-{y}^{3})\\,j-2yz\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F)=3∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2yx+{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5-{y}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-2yz) \\\\  & =2y+2x-3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2x-3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F) & =3∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =3(2x-3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6x-9{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2y+2x-9{y}^{2}"] ["math" "6x-3{y}^{2}"] ["math" "6x-9{y}^{2}"] ["math" "6y+6x-3{y}^{2}"] ["math" "9x-9{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6x-9{y}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,i-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F+G) & =∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))"] ["math" "-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)"] ["math" "2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))"] ["math" "2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)"] ["math" "4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\cdot (2F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={e}^{5x}\\,i+y{e}^{3y}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =∇\\cdot (2F)+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{5x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{3y}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2\\cdot (5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y})+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =10{e}^{5x}+2{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13{e}^{5x}+3{e}^{3y}"] ["math" "13{e}^{5x}+4{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}"] ["math" "13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}"] ["math" "7{e}^{5x}+3{e}^{3y}"] ["math" "7{e}^{5x}-4{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F-2G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}y\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=xy+{y}^{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2\\cdot (xy+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2xy-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y(1-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2y(1+2x+y)"] ["math" "2y(1-y)"] ["math" "y(1-{y}^{2})"] ["math" "y(2+x-y)"] ["math" "y(2+{y}^{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2y(1-y)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=x{e}^{2x}\\,i-y{e}^{2x}\\,j+x{z}^{2}\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)=\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}+2x{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2x}+2xz \\\\  & =2x{e}^{2x}+2xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F) & =\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2x{e}^{2x}+2xz) \\\\  & =x{e}^{2x}+xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1+2x){e}^{2x}+2xz"] ["math" "(1+x){e}^{2x}+xz"] ["math" "2x{e}^{2x}+{z}^{2}"] ["math" "2{e}^{2x}+z"] ["math" "x{e}^{2x}+xz"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x{e}^{2x}+xz"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩\\cdot ⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+2{cos}^{2}⁡z+4{sin}^{2}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-2{sin}^{2}⁡z \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2({sin}^{2}⁡z+{cos}^{2}⁡z) \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2"] ["math" "xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xz+2y"] ["math" "xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+xz"] ["math" "xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+x{z}^{2}+2"] ["math" "yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩$ and $f(x,y)=2x,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2,0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{3x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y{e}^{3x})=3{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x}={e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =2x({e}^{3x})+⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0⟩ \\\\  & =2x{e}^{3x}+2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2{x}^{2}+2x+1){e}^{3x}"] ["math" "(3x+1){e}^{3x}"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1){e}^{3x}"] ["math" "2(x+1){e}^{3x}"] ["math" "2(x+3){e}^{3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(x+1){e}^{3x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨-{x}^{2},\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y)={y}^{2},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨0,2y⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})=-2x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(-2x+y)+⟨-{x}^{2},\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2y⟩ \\\\  & =-2x{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}+{y}^{3} \\\\  & =2{y}^{3}-2x{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}(y-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x{y}^{2}(y+1)"] ["math" "2{y}^{2}(y+2x)"] ["math" "2{y}^{2}(y-x)"] ["math" "2{y}^{3}+2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}"] ["math" "2{y}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{y}^{2}(y-x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨xy,y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}(y+1)+⟨xy,y⟩\\cdot ⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩ \\\\  & =xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y} \\\\  & =3xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y} \\\\  & =x(3y+1){e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x(3y+1){e}^{y}"] ["math" "x(xy-1){e}^{y}"] ["math" "x(y+1){e}^{y}"] ["math" "x(y-1){e}^{y}"] ["math" "x({y}^{2}+x){e}^{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-131288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(3y+1){e}^{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$ and $f(x,y)=3y,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨0,3⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =3y(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3⟩ \\\\  & =9y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+0+12y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "def2a6d4c48b0b90b4a6f6395bd2f89cff616f309bdb346c7ccd3f5bdfebfb85"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "13y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "3y(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "q-105647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/state.json" "file_sha256" "99d4340eb0fd47a75940a74e408b0cff9ba5a33d98b0a6b283eb6e2c7da8af2f"} {"question" "e-8742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/example-8742.json" "file_sha256" "5b59d0acf741cefcb0721ceacd177108361f53e1e7de814de120faea7fff6e75"} {"question" "e-8742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot (F)+∇\\cdot (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x+x-2y \\\\  & =3x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =(3x-2y)-3\\cdot (x+y) \\\\  & =-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/example-8742.json" "file_sha256" "5b59d0acf741cefcb0721ceacd177108361f53e1e7de814de120faea7fff6e75"} {"question" "e-8928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x},$ calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/example-8928.json" "file_sha256" "3722ca48d770494248ccf13157e43c579b4223453a84ca8dc4b55285d88fafd0"} {"question" "e-8928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+  \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x)+⟨\\frac{1}{x},xy⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073221/example-8928.json" "file_sha256" "3722ca48d770494248ccf13157e43c579b4223453a84ca8dc4b55285d88fafd0"}] "usage" {"e-8928" [] "q-105633" [] "e-8742" [] "q-105651" []} "basis" 2679 "retractions" [[17592186179840 :question/problem "Calculate $∇ \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$F = xe^{2x}i - ye^{2x}j + xz^{2}k$."] [17592186179841 :question/problem "Given that $F(x, y, z) = ⟨e^{3x},-2ye^{3x}⟩$ and $f(x, y) = 2x$, calculate $∇ \\cdot (fF)$."] [17592186179477 :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$, where\n$\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y$."] [17592186179477 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (F - 3G) &= ∇ \\cdot (F) + ∇ \\cdot (-3G) \\\\\n&= ∇ \\cdot F - 3∇ \\cdot G\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}$. In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + y) + \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy - y^{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x + x - 2y \\\\\n&= 3x - 2y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (F - 3G) &= ∇ \\cdot F - 3∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= (3x - 2y) - 3 \\cdot (x + y) \\\\\n&=-5y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186179479 :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x}$, calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F)$."] [17592186179479 :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+ \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇f &= ⟨ - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}, 0⟩, \\\\\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x}) + \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy) =-\\frac{1}{x^{2}} + x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF) &= f∇ \\cdot F + F \\cdot ∇f \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}} + x) + ⟨\\frac{1}{x}, xy⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}, 0⟩ \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{x^{3}} + 1 - \\frac{1}{x^{3}} \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{2}{x^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186177041 17592186177042 17592186177043 17592186177044 17592186177045 17592186177047 17592186177048 17592186177049 17592186177050 17592186177051] "immutable_fields" [[17592186177040 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177040 :answer-field/id] [17592186177040 :answer-field/key] [17592186177040 :answer-field/type] [17592186177046 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177046 :answer-field/id] [17592186177046 :answer-field/key] [17592186177046 :answer-f